Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 03:14:02 2026 +0000

    BG1 interactive demo: fetch from the Silver Edition demo CD (archive.org bg-demo went dark)
    
    archive.org/details/bg-demo is now dark (metadata is_dark, no files; its
    item servers answer 403 too), so the candidate could not be fetched and
    BGDemo.exe was on no box. The same 1.0.0 demo ships on the Forgotten
    Realms Archives Silver Edition's Baldur's Gate demo CD, whose Redump image
    is in the live Interplay collection item 20230723_20230723_0858 (the
    Chapters I & II demo already comes from it).
    
    The entry now fetches that zip (sha1 df6c2f77...), converts the raw
    MODE1/2352 .bin with extractRawMode1Cd, and runs the existing unshield /
    copy / Baldur.ini steps under cd/. The disc is plain ISO 9660 (uppercase
    names), unlike the old ISO, so the CD1 and override files are copied one by
    one to the mixed-case names lib/apps.js mounts (15 files). The image itself
    differs from the old ISO (different dump), but BGDemo.exe is byte-identical
    to the pinned SHA-256 ed7f1efd... and its icon to the tracked PNG.
    
    Boat bx_zd7xmafa: fresh fetch READY (needs unshield installed), all files
    in place, --app=baldurs_gate_interactive_demo reaches the Interactive Demo
    main menu. baldurs_gate_interactive_demo returns to
    lib/app-icon-manifest.json, which is what tools/extract-app-icons.js writes
    when the fixture is present.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

